From ba74b2d919079edefebba5c19ec09cd627ca3689 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:04:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] integrations: bound provider response reads and stop
 echoing raw bodies

Model providers, PC*MILER and Ramp read whole response bodies with
io.ReadAll, so a provider (or anything an integration's base URL pointed
at) could stream an unbounded body into memory. PC*MILER also copied up
to 256 bytes of any error body into its error text, which the connection
test shows the user.

httpsafe gains ReadBody, which reads up to a limit and fails with
ErrResponseTooLarge past it instead of truncating, plus the helpers the
integration clients share: ValidateServiceURL, RedactURLError,
UpstreamErrorMessage and UpstreamMessage. Model calls cap a reply at
64 MiB and an error reply at 1 MiB, PC*MILER at 16 MiB and 64 KiB, Ramp
pages at 8 MiB. A PC*MILER error now carries only the provider's own
error message field, sanitized and bounded, never the raw body.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L7Gd5v8t2y7WHswGwtgbrn
