From bed4488f71cb5172ea5cbdac341151bf4be5557f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:01:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] integrations: route integration clients through httpsafe
 and validate base URLs on save

An integration's baseUrl was saved without validation and every
integration client (connection testers, PC*MILER, Resend, Postmark,
Ramp, OANDA, EIA, Samsara) used a plain net/http client, so an admin
could point one at loopback, a private network or the cloud metadata
endpoint and read the reply back through the connection test, the
exchange-rate error or the email message's last error.

UpdateConfig now refuses a URL field that is not https to a public host
name (no credentials, query or fragment, no reserved suffix such as
.internal or .local); carrier intelligence keeps its stricter host
allowlist. Every client defaults to httpsafe, whose dialer re-checks
each resolved address and turns redirects off; tests inject their own
client. Upstream error text reaches users and stored fields only as the
provider's own error message field, sanitized and bounded; raw bodies
never do. Ramp refuses a next-page link on another host, so its bearer
token never leaves the configured origin. Response bodies are bounded
(OANDA 4 MiB, EIA 8 MiB, testers 1 MiB, email 1 MiB, Samsara 32 MiB)
and an oversized one is an error. Transport errors from EIA, the
testers and Google Maps drop the URL query, so API keys sent as query
parameters no longer reach logs or errors.

