+## Outbound calls
+
+- **Where a call may go.** A URL a tenant can set (an integration's base URL, a partner
+  endpoint) is validated when it is saved (`httpsafe.ValidateServiceURL`) and is called only
+  through an `httpsafe` client, whose dialer re-checks every resolved address and follows no
+  redirect. A client library takes an `*http.Client` and defaults to one (`shared/pcmiler`).
+  A reply never chooses the next address: a next-page link or an async receipt URL is used only
+  on the configured origin (`rampconnector`, `editransport.InboundAsyncMDNURL`).
+- **How much is read.** `httpsafe.ReadBody` with a limit sized to the response; past it is an
+  error, never a silent truncation.
+- **What comes back to a person.** Upstream text reaches a user or a stored field only as
+  `httpsafe.UpstreamErrorMessage` of the body, never the body; a transport error whose URL
+  carries a key in its query goes through `httpsafe.RedactURLError` before it is logged.
+- **Secrets follow their destination.** A save that changes where a write-only secret is sent
+  (a `configspec.Field` that `IsDestination`, an SFTP host, a portal's domains) keeps no stored
+  secret: the person enters it again (`secretconfig.Codec.Merge`, `aiprovider.SameCredentialTarget`).
